        Translating text is simple and takes just seconds:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>Visit the <a href="/">englishtoburmese.com homepage</a>.</li>
        <li>Type or paste your English text into the <strong>English</strong> input box. You can enter up to 20,000 characters per request.</li>
        <li>Click the burgundy <strong>Translate</strong> button or press the keyboard shortcut <code>Ctrl + Enter</code>.</li>
        <li>The translated Burmese script will appear instantly in the adjacent output pane.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Copy Burmese</strong> to copy the Unicode text directly to your clipboard.</li>
      </ol>

      <div class="callout-box">
        <p>
          <strong>Pro-Tip for English to Burmese translation sentences:</strong> Break long paragraphs into shorter, one-idea sentences. Avoid overly dense compound clauses or modern slang, which machine engines often translate literally.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Step 4: Translate English to Burmese Audio &amp; Voice Dictation</h2>
