      <h2>Common Pitfalls to Avoid</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Don't rely on Zawgyi converters:</strong> Always save and export files in UTF-8 Unicode. Converting back and forth between Zawgyi and Unicode causes text fragmentation and search indexing problems.</li>
        <li><strong>Avoid ambiguous idioms:</strong> English idioms like "barking up the wrong tree" or "raining cats and dogs" will confuse automated machine translators. Rephrase to plain English (e.g., "raining heavily") before translating.</li>
        <li><strong>Always verify important legal and medical documents:</strong> Automated machine translation is fantastic for drafts, study notes, travel, and personal communication. For court filings, visa paperwork, or hospital records, always have a qualified bilingual human review your work. Check our <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a> for details.</li>
      </ol>

